# Document user-facing changes

Any new or changed command, alias, keybinding, or installed package must be documented
in the same change. A feature that is not in `welcome` does not exist to the user.

| Change | Update |
|--------|--------|
| Shell alias or function | [home/.bashrc](../../home/.bashrc) + [home/.welcome.md](../../home/.welcome.md) |
| Script in `home/.local/bin/` | [home/.welcome.md](../../home/.welcome.md) + [README.md](../../README.md) shell table |
| Readline / fzf key | `.inputrc` or `.bashrc`, the key-bindings section of `aliases()`, and `welcome` |
| GNOME `Super+…` shortcut | [scripts/setup-gnome.sh](../../scripts/setup-gnome.sh) summary output, [README.md](../../README.md), [REFRESHER.md](../../REFRESHER.md), `welcome` |
| Kitty map | [config/kitty/kitty.conf](../../config/kitty/kitty.conf) + `welcome` |
| New package | [PACKAGES.md](../../PACKAGES.md) row with purpose and related commands |

## Rules

- `PACKAGES.md` is the single catalog of package purposes. `aliases()` must not grow a
  second package description list — it points at `packages` instead.
- `PACKAGES.md` is read in the shell through `~/.packages.md` (a link to
  `home/.packages.md` → `../PACKAGES.md`). New top-level home files must be added to the
  file list in [scripts/link-dotfiles.sh](../../scripts/link-dotfiles.sh).
- Do not bind `Super+H` (Pop Shell uses it for focus-left). Minimize is `Super+Shift+N`.
- Keep custom GNOME keybinding paths and the `custom-keybindings` array in sync in
  `setup-gnome.sh`; an entry missing from the array silently does nothing.
